data: {"sections":[{"section_id":"cause_title","type":"template","content":"IN THE COURT OF DISTRICT & SESSIONS JUDGE\nAT Patna\n\nCriminal Miscellaneous Case No. _____ of 2026\n\nIN THE MATTER OF:\n\nRajan Kumar\nS/o Shri Mohan Kumar\nAge: 32 years\nR/o Village Danapur, District Patna, Bihar\n                                              ... Applicant\n\nVersus\n\nState of Bihar through the District Magistrate / S.P., Patna\n                                              ... Opposite Party","alignment":"center"},{"section_id":"application_heading","type":"template","content":"APPLICATION FOR Regular Bail UNDER SECTION 480 OF THE BHARATIYA NAGARIK SURAKSHA SANHITA, 2023","alignment":"center"},{"section_id":"addressing_clause","type":"template","content":"TO,\nTHE HONOURABLE DISTRICT & SESSIONS JUDGE,\nPatna\n\nMOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"body","type":"ai_generated","content":"1. That the Applicant has been falsely implicated in FIR No. 124/2026 dated 15.03.2026, registered at Police Station Kotwali, under Sections 303 and 351 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, and seeks regular bail from this Hon'ble Court as the matter involves both bailable and non-bailable offences.\n\n2. That the Applicant submits that he has been falsely implicated in the aforesaid FIR due to a long-standing land dispute with the Complainant. The instant case is nothing but a deliberate attempt by the Complainant to settle scores and harass the Applicant by misusing the process of law.\n\n3. That the Applicant categorically denies the allegations levelled against him and submits that he was not present at the time of the alleged incident. The Applicant has credible witnesses who can establish his alibi and prove his innocence beyond any shadow of doubt.\n\n4. That the Applicant was arrested on 16.03.2026 and has been languishing in judicial custody since then without any justifiable reason. The continued detention of the Applicant is violative of his fundamental right to liberty guaranteed under Article 21 of the Constitution of India.\n\n5. That the Applicant is a law-abiding citizen with no previous criminal antecedents and has never been involved in any criminal activity whatsoever. He is a respectable member of society and poses no threat to the peace and tranquility of the area.\n\n6. That the Applicant has deep roots in the community and has no intention or inclination to flee from justice or abscond. He is ready and willing to cooperate with the investigation and abide by any conditions that this Hon'ble Court may deem fit to impose.\n\n7. That the Applicant has been fully cooperating with the investigating authorities and has not hampered the investigation in any manner. He is prepared to make himself available as and when required by the investigating officer.\n\n8. That the investigation is pending and there is no likelihood of the Applicant tampering with evidence or influencing witnesses if released on bail. The continued custody of the Applicant serves no useful purpose and amounts to pre-trial punishment.\n\n9. That the Applicant undertakes to abide by all conditions that may be imposed by this Hon'ble Court and guarantees his presence before the trial court as and when required during the pendency of the trial.\n\n10. That in view of the false implication, lack of criminal antecedents, absence of flight risk, and the Applicant's willingness to cooperate with the investigation, the interests of justice would be best served by granting bail to the Applicant."},{"section_id":"prayer","type":"template","content":"PRAYER\n\nIt is, therefore, most humbly prayed that this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to:\n\na) Grant Regular Bail to the Applicant, Rajan Kumar, in connection with FIR No. 124/2026 dated 15.03.2026, PS Kotwali, under Section 480 of BNSS, 2023, on such terms and conditions as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit;\n\nb) Pass such other orders as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the facts and circumstances of the case, in the interest of justice.\n\nAnd for this act of kindness, the applicant shall ever pray.","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"verification","type":"template","content":"VERIFICATION\n\nI, Rajan Kumar, the Applicant herein above named, do hereby verify that the contents of the above application are true and correct to the best of my knowledge and belief and nothing material has been concealed therefrom.\n\nVerified at Patna on this _____ day of _________, 2026.\n\nDEPONENT\n\n\n_________________________\nRajan Kumar\n(Applicant)","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"advocate_block","type":"template","content":"THROUGH:\n\n_________________________\nSmoke Test\nAdvocate\nEnrollment No. ____________________\n\nPlace: Patna\nDate: 06 May 2026","alignment":"right"},{"section_id":"disclaimer","type":"template","content":"AI-assisted draft — verify with applicable law before filing. Lawie does not provide legal advice.","alignment":"center","style":"footer_small_gray"}]}

